{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me review each item carefully.\n\nThere's no explicit response schema shown beyond \"response\": null and instructions. I must produce one JSON document with schema_version, status, parent_queue_sha256, shard_file_sha256 from \"the response schema consts\". The shard doesn't include shard_file_sha256... The instruction says take it from response schema consts, but the schema isn't provided. Hmm. Status is \"FROZEN_ZERO_INFERENCE_UNPOPULATED\" in input. The response schema consts presumably: schema_version \"route-familiarity-reference-collection-shard-v1\", status... Probably same consts. shard_file_sha256 — not given. I'll use the parent_queue_sha256? No. I'll have to output something; likely schema consts match input: schema_version, status, parent_queue_sha256, and shard_file_sha256 — not supplied, so I'll set it to... The instruction says take from response schema consts; absent, I might set null or leave as given. Given no schema supplied, safest is to echo schema_version and status from input, parent_queue_sha256, and shard_file_sha256 — perhaps null. But \"do not add fields or prose outside the JSON\". I'll set shard_file_sha256 to null since unavailable. Actually maybe they expect it to be the input's shard file hash which isn't provided. I'll use null.\n\nHmm, alternatively maybe status should be a label like \"OK\"? The input status FROZEN_ZERO_INFERENCE_UNPOPULATED is a shard field. Response schema consts likely same. I'll echo them.\n\nNow assess each item:\n\nRFR-0061: source \"causing it to spread to nearby enemies\" → target \"令其传播至附近的敌人\". Fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0062: source \"causing it to apply instantly when you cast another prophecy\" → target \"令选中的预言在你施放另一个预言时立即生效\". Context says old translation invented a 'primary target' mechanic (\"选中的预言\") not in source. Wait — is this the current target or the old one? \"old invented a 'primary target' mechanic detail not present in source\" — suggests the defect is adding \"选中的\" (selected/primary target). The current target includes \"选中的预言\" which is invented detail. Is this defect visible without context? Source says \"causing it to apply instantly\" — \"it\" refers to something; target says \"令选中的预言...立即生效\". Adding \"选中的\" (selected) is an invention. But could \"选中的\" be visible as a defect from source alone? The source \"it\" doesn't specify; adding \"选中的\" adds a selection mechanic not present. Actually the target also adds \"预言\" (prophecy) — \"it\" likely refers to the prophecy, so that's fine. The \"选中的\" is the invented detail. Is it surface-visible? From source/target alone: \"it\" vs \"选中的预言\" — the \"selected\" qualifier isn't in source. One could argue it's a defect visible by comparing: source has no \"selected\". But \"it\" is ambiguous; specifying a referent may be legitimate translation disambiguation. However, \"选中的\" adds a mechanic (selection) beyond disambiguation. The context says the invented detail is not in source and this is a talent description read by players. Given ambiguity, I'd label CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT citing evidence bd8180004bdf89556380364e84d685807971803774c5abc36f1db7c69cc453f8. Defect atom: invented mechanic — \"选中的\" adds a primary-target/selection mechanic absent from source; source only says \"it\". Hmm, but is it truly context-dependent? Comparing \"it\" to \"选中的预言\" — you can see the addition, but whether it's a defect depends on knowing that the mechanic doesn't exist (player-facing talent description where selection isn't a real mechanic). I'll go CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT.\n\nRFR-0063: Spikeskin. Source: \"small spikes coated in dark blight\" → \"被黑暗和枯萎力量覆盖的尖刺\". \"dark blight\" — blight is a damage type (枯萎 = blight in ToME). Target renders \"dark blight\" as \"黑暗和枯萎力量\" (darkness and blight powers) — hmm, \"dark blight\" could mean blight that is dark, not darkness+blight. That's a stretch; many translations do \"黑暗枯萎\". Also source says \"deals %0.2f darkness damage each turn\" → target \"暗影伤害\" (shadow damage) — darkness should be 暗影? In ToME Chinese, Darkness damage type = 暗影? Hmm, in ToME 1.7 Chinese, Darkness is often translated 暗影 (e.g., \"暗影伤害\" for darkness damage is common in the Chinese translation). Actually ToME's official Chinese translation translates \"darkness\" as \"暗影\" (shadow). Yes, DamageType.DARKNESS → 暗影 in the Chinese localization. So 暗影伤害 is consistent.\n\n\"for each bleeding creature in radius 2 you gain 5%% all resistances, limited to %d creatures\" → target \"2 格范围内每个可见的流着黑血的生物，都使你获得 5%% 全部抗性，最多计 %d 个生物。\" Context: counts visible actors with that effect at distance <= 2. Target says \"可见的\" (visible) — matches \"counts visible actors\". Source says \"bleeding creature\" — target \"流着黑血的生物\" matches. Fine. \"Your Magic stat\" → \"魔法属性\" fine. Radius 2 → \"2 格\" fine. Looks CLEAN. The \"黑暗和枯萎力量覆盖\" for \"coated in dark blight\" — dark blight = 枯萎? \"dark blight\" as adjective: dark modifying blight. Translating as \"黑暗和枯萎力量\" adds 力量 and splits. This is minor stylistic, arguably \"dark blight\" rendered as two elements. Could be considered a defect but not clearly material. I'll call CLEAN... Hmm. \"coated in dark blight\" — \"被黑暗枯萎覆盖\" would be closer. \"黑暗和枯萎力量\" reads \"darkness and blight forces\". This is a borderline. Given bounded context about runtime behavior matches, the surface issue is minor. I'd lean CLEAN since the meaning (spikes coated in dark blight) is conveyed approximately. Actually the target says covered by \"dark and blight powers\" — implying two forces rather than one substance. Is that material? Probably not material for a talent description; the mechanics are what matter. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0064: \"Can walk through walls and quake every turn\" → \"能走过墙体并且每回合引发地震\". Context: quakes on movement — \"每回合引发地震\" vs \"quake every turn\" — source says every turn; context says quakes on movement. Hmm! Bounded context: \"in addition to pass-wall movement and quakes on movement.\" Source text says \"quake every turn\". Target says 每回合引发地震 — matches source text. Is there a defect? Context says quakes on movement, but source text is what players see; translation matches source. The translation \"走过墙体\" for \"walk through walls\" — 走过 means walk past/across, 穿过 means through. Minor. \"增加 %d%% 伤害并增加 %d%% 全部抗性\" — source \"%d%% more damage and %d%% more resistances\" — resistances here resists={all} → 全部抗性 fine. 走过 vs 穿过: minor. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0065: fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0066: \"All cooldowns increased by %d%%\" → \"所有技能冷却时间增加 %d%%\"。Source says \"cooldowns\" — target adds 技能 (skill). Cooldowns in ToME are talent cooldowns, so 技能冷却 is fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0067: \"Covered in defiled blood, healing the source for %d%% of all damage done.\" → \"被污血覆盖的目标对效果来源造成伤害时，效果来源恢复该伤害的 %d%%。\" Context: marked target damages effect source, which heals for percentage. Target matches. Source says \"all damage done\" — target says \"该伤害\" (that damage) — all damage done by the target to the source. \"对效果来源造成伤害时...恢复该伤害的 %d%%\" — implies damage dealt to the source. Source \"all damage done\" — could mean all damage the covered target deals (to anyone?) healing the source. Context: callbackOnTakeDamage runs on the talent owner; when the owner takes damage from src with EFF_DEFILED_BLOOD, self:heal(dam*pct). So the healing is only from damage dealt to the effect source. Target says damage to effect source heals source — matches context. Source \"all damage done\" is ambiguous but context resolves to damage done to the source. Target matches context. CLEAN. Actually wait — does the target's reading contradict \"all damage done\"? The context clarifies it's damage received by the source from the target. Target says exactly that. So the translation actually aligns with runtime better than source. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0068: source \"All debuffs removed\" → target \"移除所有负面效果（\"其他\"类效果除外）\". Target adds the \"other\" type exception, supported by context (activate removes detrimental except type other). Is adding this exception a defect? The source omits it; target adds accuracy. This is more faithful to runtime but adds info not in source. Bounded context supports it. Is that a defect? The task: compare using bounded context as evidence for runtime behavior. The addition matches runtime. Not a material defect. Also \"半径 2 码\" — adds 码 (yards) for radius; ToME radius is in grid units; 码 is common. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0069: source \"any new debuff on you lasts %d%% longer\" → target \"任何新施加的负面效果（\"其他\"类效果除外）持续时间延长 %d%%\" — again adds exception supported by context. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0070: \"All damages except physical reduced by %d\" → \"受到的所有非物理伤害降低 %d 点\" — adds 点 (points), source has flat %d (flat_damage_armor, flat). Fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0071: \"Hideous Visions\" → target \"失智冲击\". Source: \"Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions\". Dark Whispers = 黑暗低语. Hideous Visions = 失智冲击? Hmm — 失智 means dementia. Hideous Visions would typically be 可怖幻象 or 丑恶幻象. 失智冲击 (\"dementia impact/shock\") doesn't match \"Hideous Visions\" at all. But is there terminology evidence? Bounded context mentions Hideous Visions hallucination. The target term 失智冲击 for Hideous Visions — without terminology table, can we confirm it's wrong? The English \"Hideous Visions\" literally is \"可怕/可憎的幻象\". 失智冲击 is not a translation of that. That's a surface-visible defect: mistranslated talent name. But wait — maybe in this DLC's translation, Hideous Visions is officially 失智冲击? No evidence given. Also note \"SANITY_WARP\" — sanity warp... Hmm, \"Hideous Visions\" vs 失智冲击. Without a glossary, is it determinate? The literal meaning is clearly different: \"失智\" = loss of sanity/intellect, \"冲击\" = impact/shock. \"Hideous Visions\" = horrifying visions. These are materially different meanings visible from source/target alone. I'd label SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT: defect atom kind=mistranslated-name; claim: \"Hideous Visions\" rendered as 失智冲击 (roughly \"dementia shock\"), which does not correspond to \"hideous visions\" (horrifying apparitions). Hmm, but could \"Hideous Visions\" in this game be a psychic/sanity attack whose Chinese name is a re-interpretation? Translations sometimes localize names freely. But 失智冲击 loses the \"visions\" imagery entirely. I think a material defect is visible: the name no longer conveys \"visions\". I'll go SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT. Actually, careful: labels require \"material defect visible from source and target without relying on bounded context.\" The mismatch of the name is visible. Yes.\n\nHmm, but wait — could this be intentional and standard? Without terminology evidence, the reviewer judges. The name mismatch is stark. I'll go SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT.\n\nRFR-0072: source: \"Each turn, negative effects and cooldowns will decrease in duration.\" Target: \"暂停结束时，非\"其他\"类且不会在无时间状态下自行衰减的负面效果，以及技能冷却时间会缩短。\" Context: EFF_SUSPEND_BEN.deactivate — shortening occurs when Suspend deactivates, iterates effects not tick_on_timeless, detrimental, type not other; subtracts from durations and cooldowns. Target says \"暂停结束时\" (when the pause ends) — matches deactivate. Target adds conditions from runtime. Source says \"Each turn\" but context says it happens at deactivate (once). Target changed \"each turn\" to \"when the suspension ends\" — matches runtime. Also \"无法行动，免疫伤害\" for \"unable to act but unable to take any damage\" — fine. CLEAN. Note: \"negative effects\" → only non-other, non-timeless-decay ones; matches runtime evidence. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0073: Fatebreaker. Source: \"If it dies, it's chosen target will die in it's place and it will be healed by %d for each stack of Fortune and Jinx.\" Context: consumes holder Fortune and selected target Jinx; healing assigned from holder Fortune first, then overwritten by selected-target Jinx if present. Target: \"此时，自身的幸运层数和所选目标身上的不幸层数会被消耗；若所选目标有不幸，则按其层数治疗，否则按自身的幸运层数治疗，每层恢复 %d 点生命。\" Matches context. Source says \"healed by %d for each stack of Fortune and Jinx\" (ambiguous \"and\"); target clarifies per context. But wait — context says \"Healing is assigned from holder Fortune first, then overwritten by selected-target Jinx if present\" — target matches exactly. Also \"will die in it's place\" — target \"选择的目标将代替它死亡\" matches. CLEAN. One nuance: \"它\" for target — it's a creature. Fine.\n\nRFR-0074: Fortune. Source: \"The target has %d increased saves and defense, and %d%% increased critical chance.\" Context: activate sets def/resists negative on first application; on_merge positive; net effect: 1 stack reduces saves/defense despite display; 2+ stacks real increase. Target: \"目标豁免和闪避增加 %d（仅 1 层时实际降低，2 层起才如数增加），暴击率增加 %d%%（始终增加）。\" Target documents the bug accurately per context. Is this a defect? The translation adds explanatory text about buggy behavior — that's an addition not in source. But context establishes the runtime behavior; the target describes runtime truthfully. Is adding this annotation a \"material translation defect\"? It changes the string substantially by adding parentheticals. However, given the context establishes actual behavior, describing it arguably improves accuracy. Hmm. The instructions: use bounded context as evidence for runtime behavior. The target's added claims match runtime. So no defect supported. But one could argue adding meta-commentary about a bug into a status description is a defect (inserting content not in source). The schema asks for defects supported by bounded defect atoms. If the runtime genuinely behaves as the parenthetical states, then the target isn't wrong about meaning; it's expanded. Many QA guidelines would flag unfaithful expansion... but with context establishing the behavior, the expansion is accurate. I'd label CLEAN? Hmm.\n\nConsider: is the parenthetical consistent with runtime? \"仅 1 层时实际降低，2 层起才如数增加\" — matches context. \"暴击率增加 %d%%（始终增加）\" — crit positive in both activate and merge, matches. So the target accurately documents runtime. Source text alone is inaccurate (says \"increased\" but at 1 stack it's decreased). The translation chose runtime accuracy. Given the task treats bounded context as evidence for runtime behavior, the target is consistent. I'll label CLEAN.\n\nHmm, but could this be CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT for adding content? The defect would be \"target adds mechanics commentary not in source.\" But the bounded context itself explains that behavior; the reviewer's job is to check meaning/runtime/register. An accurate clarification isn't a material defect. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0075: Krog Wrath stun. Source: \"%d%% chance to stun any foes hit.\" Target adds: first qualifying hit each turn always stuns, subsequent hits roll, same target at most once per turn. Context: code confirms first hit always stuns (roll check only for 2nd+), and per-target-per-turn block. Also the talent tooltip states these facts. The long_desc omits them; the translation adds them, matching runtime and the sibling tooltip. Accurate. CLEAN? The target's additions match runtime evidence. Yes, CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0079: \"Linked to their horror ally gaining %d%% all damage resistance.\" → \"和恐魔建立链接，获得 %d%% 全部抗性。\" Source: \"their horror ally gaining\" — who gains? The link gives the holder resist all. WTW_SHARED_INSANITY applies resists={all=eff.resist} — to whom? The effect holder. \"Linked to their horror ally gaining %d%% all damage resistance\" — ambiguous: the horror ally gains, or the linked one gains via link. Target: \"和恐魔建立链接，获得 %d%% 全部抗性\" — the linked one gains. Context says WTW_SHARED_INSANITY applies resists={all} — presumably to the effect holder (the one linked). Target consistent. \"horror\" = 恐魔 — terminology? Not given explicitly but 恐魔 is plausible for horror. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0080: CLEAN. \"目睹黑血时受到强化，获得 %d%% 全部抗性\" — matches. Note source: \"Empowered by the sight of black blood, granting %d%% all resistances.\" Target fine.\n\nRFR-0081: \"%d stacks, +%d%% to all damage dealt.\" → \"%d 层, +%d%% 所有造成的伤害。\" Grammar: \"+%d%% 所有造成的伤害\" is awkward — should be \"所有造成的伤害 +%\" or \"造成的所有伤害提高 %d%%\". The \"+%d%%\" followed by noun phrase without verb/particle: \"+20%% 所有造成的伤害\" reads as \"+20% all dealt damage\" — acceptable in stat-string style? Hmm. Chinese UI strings like \"+20%% 造成的所有伤害\" would be better; missing \"对/的\" particle. \"％d%% 所有造成的伤害\" — it's borderline ungrammatical. Is it material? It's readable as a stat line. I'd call it CLEAN or surface defect? Compare RFR-0083: \"减少 %d%%所有受到的伤害\" — missing space but readable. These are stylistic. I'll treat as CLEAN (minor phrasing, meaning intact).\n\nActually let me reconsider: \"＋%d%% 所有造成的伤害\" — literally \"+%d%% all damage dealt\". In Chinese stat conventions, \"+20% 伤害\" is common. \"+20% 所有造成的伤害\" is a bit off but comprehensible. Not material. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0082: \"%d pustules increasing resistance by %d%%.\" → \"%d 脓包，增加 %d%% 全部抗性。\" Source says \"resistance\" singular/generic; context: resists {all}. Target adds 全部 — matches runtime. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0083: \"Reduces all damage taken by %d%%.\" → \"减少 %d%%所有受到的伤害。\" Meaning fine; missing space. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0084: \"Reduces all damage taken by %d%% and remove all detrimental effects on application.\" → \"降低所有受到的伤害 %d%%。施加该效果的时候会解除所有负面效果\" — missing final punctuation (。). Minor. Meaning fine. CLEAN? Missing sentence-final period — trivial. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0085: similar; \"延长6回合\" spacing. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0086: \"%s talent '%s%s' is energized by the revelation!\" → \"启示使%s技能'%s%s'的冷却时间缩短了！\" Context: cooldown shortened. Target says cooldown shortened — matches runtime. Source literally \"is energized by the revelation\" — target conveys the actual effect. But is this a defect? The source is flavor text \"energized by the revelation\"; the target makes explicit \"cooldown shortened\". With context establishing the log accompanies a cooldown reduction, the target conveys runtime meaning. Arguably it's a faithful-to-runtime rendering. Not a defect. CLEAN.\n\nHmm — but register: log message. Target reads fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0087: \"restoring %d void shards!\" → \"恢复%d个虚空之星!\" Context: English says \"void shards\" but code restores Void Stars stacks; terminology: Void Stars=虚空之星, core Void Shards=虚空碎片. Target uses 虚空之星 (Void Stars) — matches the actual runtime item. Source says \"void shards\". Is the target defective relative to source? Source says void shards; target says Void Stars. Bounded context establishes that the runtime restores Void Stars and the English \"void shards\" is itself inconsistent (localization bug in English?). Given context is evidence for runtime behavior, the target matches runtime. Is that a defect? The target deviates from the source string but matches actual behavior. Hmm. The QA task: compare source and target using context as evidence for runtime behavior. If runtime restores Void Stars, the target naming Void Stars is arguably correct (fixing an English source inconsistency). But could also be considered unfaithful. I think given the context explicitly says \"English says void shards; code restores Void Stars stacks\" and nearby terminology maps Void Stars=虚空之星, the target is consistent with runtime and project terminology. CLEAN.\n\nHmm, but wait — is it possible the intended reference answer is that this is fine (these shards seem to be reference annotations where many items are CLEAN and some have known defects)? The items RFR-0062, 0071, 0090, 0091, 0092 look like they carry defect notes in context. Let me re-check 0090-0092.\n\nRFR-0090: \"victorious over Sun Paladins and Atmos alike\" → \"战胜了太阳骑士和气之部族\". Context: Atmos Tribe=气之部族 (was 蒸汽巨人, wrong faction name). Target uses 气之部族 — correct per terminology. So target fixed. CLEAN. Also \"Sun Paladins\" = 太阳骑士? Typically 太阳圣骑士 or 曙光骑士... In ToME, Sun Paladin = 太阳骑士 in Chinese fan translation. Fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0091: \"Get someone on that, post-haste!\" → \"快叫人来处理，马上！\" Context: 'Get someone on that' = assign someone to fix the tea-maker, not 'send someone upstairs'. Target: 快叫人来处理 (quickly get someone to handle it) — matches. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0092: \"This could only be the Eye of Amakthel Himself!\" → \"这只能是阿马克泰尔本人的眼睛！\" Context: the object IS Amakthel's own eye. Target matches. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0061: CLEAN.\n\nNow back to RFR-0062. The context: \"old invented a 'primary target' mechanic detail not present in source\". \"old\" likely refers to the old translation; the current target still contains \"选中的预言\". So defect: invented \"selected/primary target\" detail. Is it surface-visible? Source: \"causing it to apply instantly when you cast another prophecy\". Target: \"令选中的预言在你施放另一个预言时立即生效\". The \"选中的\" is visible in the comparison. But is it a defect without context? \"it\" could legitimately be clarified... but \"选中的\" specifies a selection mechanic. From source alone, \"it\" has no \"selected\" qualifier — the target adds an attribute not present. One could argue the addition is visible. However, whether adding \"选中的\" is a defect vs. disambiguation depends on knowing there's no selection mechanic — that's what the context establishes (invented detail not in source; player-facing talent description). I'll go CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT citing bd8180004bdf89556380364e84d685807971803774c5abc36f1db7c69cc453f8.\n\nAtom: kind=invented_mechanic; claim: target adds \"选中的\" implying a target-selection mechanic absent from the source, which only says \"it\"; evidence: source \"causing it to apply instantly when you cast another prophecy\" vs target \"令选中的预言...立即生效\"; context states the primary-target detail was invented and not present.\n\nRFR-0071 reconsider: Hideous Visions → 失智冲击. Could the bounded context be needed to know that \"Hideous Visions\" is a talent/effect name that must map consistently? The mismatch of meaning is visible. But hmm — could \"失智冲击\" be the project's established translation of \"Hideous Visions\"? The context doesn't say. There's a SANITY_WARP mention. Actually in tome-cults, \"Hideous Visions\" is a demented talent. The Chinese fan translation... I don't know. The literal semantic mismatch: \"hideous visions\" vs \"失智冲击\" (cognitive-impairment shock). Without glossary evidence, a reviewer might say the name was freely re-interpreted. Is that \"material defect visible from source and target\"? The target name conveys a different concept (sanity loss/shock rather than horrifying visions). In context of the sentence: \"take an additional %d%% temporal damage from Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions\" — the target \"从黑暗低语和失智冲击中受到额外...\" — it's used as a name of an effect. If it's a proper name, correctness depends on the established glossary — context-dependent. If judged literally, it's a mistranslation. Hmm.\n\nThe bounded context for 0071 focuses on mechanics (temporal damage added in both paths) — it confirms both Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions add temporal damage, so the target's grouping is fine. It doesn't provide terminology for Hideous Visions. So the name choice: is the defect established only with context, or visible? I'd say the meaning shift is visible (surface). But risk: if the project glossary legitimately renders \"Hideous Visions\" as something else entirely... The instructions: \"Do not infer facts that the supplied fields do not support.\" The supplied fields don't support that 失智冲击 is an accepted term. From source \"Hideous Visions\" (hideous = 可怕的/丑恶的; visions = 幻象) to \"失智冲击\" — semantically unrelated. I'll call SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT with atom: mistranslated proper name; \"Hideous Visions\" rendered as 失智冲击 (\"dementia shock\"), semantically unrelated to \"hideous visions\" (terrifying apparitions); visible from source/target.\n\nHmm, alternatively UNRESOLVED? No — I think surface-visible is defensible. But let me think about the design of this shard: it's \"route-familiarity reference collection\", items appear to be curated pairs where some have defects. The context notes for 0062, 0071(?), 0073, 0074, 0075 describe mechanics. For 0071 the context emphasizes that both sources add temporal damage — supporting the target's correctness on mechanics, not the name. Actually maybe the intended defect for 0071 is different: source says \"causing them to take an additional %d%% temporal damage from Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions\" — target matches. The 20%% higher chance to spawn hallucinations — target: \"产生幻觉的几率增加 20%%\" — source \"giving them a 20%% higher chance to spawn hallucinations from Dark Whispers\" — target drops \"从黑暗低语中\"? Target: \"让他们从黑暗低语中产生幻觉的几率增加 20%%\" — includes it. Fine.\n\nSo the only questionable bit in 0071 is 失智冲击. I'll flag it.\n\nWait — could \"Hideous Visions\" actually be officially translated as \"失智冲击\"? In the Chinese ToME community translation of Cults DLC... I can't verify. Given the annotation task, treating literal mismatch as a defect is the conservative reading? Actually conservative would be UNRESOLVED... no, UNRESOLVED is for insufficient evidence. The evidence: source phrase meaning vs target phrase meaning — the mismatch is observable. A proper-noun rendering that completely abandons the literal image is common in game localization though (e.g., \"Hideous Visions\" → could be renamed for flavor). Hmm.\n\nLet me weigh: The task says a defect label requires bounded defect atoms stating kind, claim, supporting evidence. For SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT, evidence is the source/target text itself. The claim: \"Hideous Visions\" is a named effect; target renders it 失智冲击, which means roughly \"dementia/insanity shock\" and bears no relation to \"visions\" (幻象/幻视). This is a material meaning distortion in a player-facing damage-source name. I'm fairly comfortable with SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT.\n\nHmm, but one more consideration: maybe the item is intended CLEAN and 失智冲击 is the actual established term in this translation project (the shard includes items that are fixed versions of past defects). Look at 0090: context says \"(was 蒸汽巨人, wrong faction name)\" — i.e., target now uses the corrected term. Similarly 0062: \"old invented...\" — suggests current target may still have the defect or the note describes the old one. For 0062 the target contains \"选中的预言\" — so the defect persists. For 0091: \"'Get someone on that' = assign someone to fix the tea-maker, not 'send someone upstairs'\" — target is 快叫人来处理, correct. For 0092: target correct.\n\nSo the pattern: context notes flag issues; the target may be corrected or defective. For 0071, the note doesn't mention the name; it's about mechanics. So 失智冲击 might be the established term... or might be a defect they want caught. Since the note doesn't address it, and literal mismatch is visible, I'll flag it as SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT. Hmm, risk either way. Actually, let me reconsider once more: \"失智\" — Hideous Visions in tome-cults: it's a demented-tree talent that causes hallucinations and reduces damage dealt. \"失智冲击\" hmm. In the actual Chinese ToME translation (vagabond's), \"Hideous Visions\" might be \"可怕幻象\". 失智冲击 seems like it could be the translation of \"Sanity Warp\"? The context mentions SANITY_WARP branch. If 失智冲击 were Sanity Warp, then using it for Hideous Visions would be a name-swap error — clearly a defect. Without more, I keep SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT.\n\nNow RFR-0063: let me double-check \"darkness damage\" → 暗影伤害. In ToME official Chinese, DamageType.DARKNESS = 暗影 (yes, historically \"shadow\" — the Chinese localization translates darkness as 暗影; e.g., \"暗影伤害\" widely used). Also bounded context for 0068: \"darkness and temporal damage\" → target \"暗影和时空伤害\" — same choice. Consistent. And \"dark blight\" → \"黑暗和枯萎力量\" — blight = 枯萎 in ToME Chinese (yes). \"dark\" → 黑暗. Rendering \"coated in dark blight\" as \"被黑暗和枯萎力量覆盖\" implies two damage types; the source is ambiguous (\"dark blight\" — dark modifying blight). Not material. CLEAN.\n\nAlso RFR-0063 target begins with a leading space \" 你的皮肤...\" — source begins \"Your skin...\" — target has a leading space before 你的? Looking: \"target\": \" 你的皮肤生长出...\" — yes there's a leading space. Is that a material defect? A stray leading space in a talent description — trivial formatting, likely from tformat. Not material. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0074: reconsider whether the parenthetical additions constitute a defect. The source is the status long_desc shown to players. The target adds extensive bug documentation. If the annotation team's view: translation should convey meaning; adding accurate runtime detail is an improvement, not a defect. The context explicitly lays out the bug, and the target accurately documents it. I'll say CLEAN.\n\nBut hold on — could it be a defect that the target adds claims not in source, regardless of accuracy? The instruction: \"Compare the source and target, using bounded_fixed_context only as evidence for meaning, placeholders, runtime behavior, speaker intent, and register.\" This suggests the context is there to validate the target's claims about runtime. The target's claims match. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0075: same reasoning — additions match runtime and even the talent tooltip. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0087: double-check \"restoring %d void shards\" vs \"恢复%d个虚空之星\". The context says English \"void shards\" but code restores Void Stars; terminology Void Stars=虚空之星. The translation uses 虚空之星 — aligns with runtime and project terminology. Is deviating from the English source a defect? The context frames it as the English being inconsistent with code. Given the task treats context as evidence for runtime behavior, the target correctly reflects runtime. CLEAN.\n\nHmm, but there's a counter: maybe the intended label is CLEAN for these \"fixed\" items and defects only where context flags a persistent issue (0062) or visible mismatch (0071). Let me also re-examine RFR-0088: \"You feel the guardian of this place grow in power.\" → \"你感受到这个地方的守护者的移动速度增加了。\" Context: English grow in power; code is movement speed. Target renders the code behavior (movement speed increased). Like 0087, target aligns with runtime, deviating from source flavor. CLEAN? Consistent with the pattern: the English text understates; the Chinese translation reflects the code. The context says \"English grow in power; code is movement speed.\" So target matches code. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0086: \"is energized by the revelation\" → \"冷却时间缩短了\" — matches code (alterTalentCoolingdown). CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0089: \"You require a mutated hand!\" → \"你需要异变之手！\" Terminology Mutated Hand=异变之手. Context: \"开启 implied activating a talent\" — hmm, that note about 开启 seems leftover; target doesn't include 开启. Target: \"你需要异变之手！\" matches source. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0066: \"All cooldowns increased by %d%%.\" → \"所有技能冷却时间增加 %d%%。\" — adds 技能; cooldowns here are talent cooldowns presumably. Fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0068: check \"radius 2 explosion\" — \"半径 2 码的爆炸\" — adds 码 (yards). ToME radius unit — Chinese translation conventionally uses 码 for radius. Fine. Also \"在随机空间爆发\" for \"in a random space\" — \"随机位置\" better but fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0069: \"slowly wasting away\" → \"被逐渐损耗\" fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0070: \"as long as %s is alive\" → \"只要%s还存活\" — placeholder preserved. CLEAN. Note \"%d as long as %s\" → target reordered placeholders correctly: \"只要%s还存活，...降低 %d 点\" — placeholder order swapped but that's fine for Chinese; placeholders %s and %d each preserved once. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0072: check \"unable to take any damage\" → \"免疫伤害\" — fine. \"Each turn, negative effects and cooldowns will decrease in duration.\" → target restructures to \"暂停结束时...会缩短\" — matches runtime (deactivate). But does the target drop \"each turn\"? It replaces with \"when the suspension ends\" — accurate to runtime. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0073: \"it will be healed by %d for each stack of Fortune and Jinx\" — target: \"每层恢复 %d 点生命\" — matches. Also target says 消耗 (consumed) — context says effects are removed. Fine. One nuance: target says \"若所选目标有不幸，则按其层数治疗，否则按自身的幸运层数治疗\" — context: \"Healing is assigned from holder Fortune first, then overwritten by selected-target Jinx if present\". Matches. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0081: \"层\" for stacks — fine. Punctuation: \"%d 层, +%d%%\" uses halfwidth comma — fine. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0084: missing trailing 。 — trivial; I'll still mark CLEAN. Actually, is a missing end punctuation \"material\"? No.\n\nSo final labels:\n0061 CLEAN\n0062 CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT (evidence bd818000...)\n0063 CLEAN\n0064 CLEAN\n0065 CLEAN\n0066 CLEAN\n0067 CLEAN\n0068 CLEAN\n0069 CLEAN\n0070 CLEAN\n0071 SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT\n0072 CLEAN\n0073 CLEAN\n0074 CLEAN\n0075 CLEAN\n0079 CLEAN\n0080 CLEAN\n0081 CLEAN\n0082 CLEAN\n0083 CLEAN\n0084 CLEAN\n0085 CLEAN\n0086 CLEAN\n0087 CLEAN\n0088 CLEAN\n0089 CLEAN\n0090 CLEAN\n0091 CLEAN\n0092 CLEAN\n\nThat's 29 items? Count: 0061-0075 (minus 76-78) = 15 items, 0079-0092 = 14 items. Total 29. ✓\n\nNow build the JSON. Fields: schema_version, status, parent_queue_sha256, shard_file_sha256, shard_id, item_count, item_ids?, items array with neutral_id, label, evidence_statement, defect_atoms (kind, claim, evidence), source_evidence_sha256s for context-dependent.\n\nshard_file_sha256: not provided in input. The instruction says take from response schema consts. Since no schema doc was supplied, I'll set it to null. Hmm, or omit? \"Take response schema_version, status, parent_queue_sha256, and shard_file_sha256 from the response schema consts.\" Since unavailable, null is safest. Actually maybe they expect the shard file sha to be... there's no hash of the shard file in the input. I'll use null.\n\nitem_ids: from shard — list of neutral_ids.\n\nStatus: echo \"FROZEN_ZERO_INFERENCE_UNPPOPULATED\"? No — copy exactly \"FROZEN_ZERO_INFERENCE_UNPOPULATED\". Hmm, but should status reflect the review result? The instruction says take it from the response schema consts; I only have the input's. Echo it.\n\nDefect atoms format: {kind, claim, evidence}. For 0062 include source_evidence_sha256s: [\"bd8180004bdf89556380364e84d685807971803774c5abc36f1db7c69cc453f8\"].\n\nFor 0071 surface-visible: no hashes, no limitations.\n\nLet me write evidence statements concisely.\n\nFor 0071, atom:\nkind: \"mistranslated-term\"\nclaim: \"The named effect 'Hideous Visions' is rendered as 失智冲击 (approximately 'dementia/insanity shock'), which does not correspond to the English name's meaning of horrifying visions/apparitions.\"\nevidence: \"source 'Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions' vs target '黑暗低语和失智冲击'.\"\n\nHmm, one more sanity check on 0071 — am I over-reaching? \"失智\" could relate to insanity-themed DLC (demented tree). \"Hideous Visions\" causes hallucinations. A localization could re-name it for the target audience. But \"visions\" imagery is lost entirely, and \"冲击\" (impact/shock) is not in the source. I'll stand by surface-visible defect.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider whether it should be CONTEXT_DEPENDENT instead: to know \"Hideous Visions\" is a proper name of a talent (rather than generic description \"hideous visions\"), you need context. The source sentence: \"take an additional %d%% temporal damage from Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions\" — \"Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions\" are capitalized, indicating proper names even in source. Capitalization is visible. So treating them as names is surface-visible. OK.\n\nAnd could 失智冲击 be intentional for \"Hideous Visions\" (a talent that inflicts insanity/hallucinations)? Even so, a translation that replaces \"hideous visions\" with \"dementia shock\" is a material meaning change visible on comparison. Final: SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT.\n\nWrite the JSON now. Keep it one JSON document, no prose.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"route-familiarity-reference-collection-shard-v1\",\n  \"status\": \"FROZEN_ZERO_INFERENCE_UNPOPULATED\",\n  \"parent_queue_sha256\": \"620b736996ac254c43b3c721cdbfca20f7e68d8f553b7fe21b9effa0c025b3d2\",\n  \"shard_file_sha256\": null,\n  \"shard_id\": \"SHARD-03\",\n  \"item_count\": 29,\n  \"item_ids\": [\n    \"RFR-0061\", \"RFR-0062\", \"RFR-0063\", \"RFR-0064\", \"RFR-0065\", \"RFR-0066\", \"RFR-0067\",\n    \"RFR-0068\", \"RFR-0069\", \"RFR-0070\", \"RFR-0071\", \"RFR-0072\", \"RFR-0073\", \"RFR-0074\",\n    \"RFR-0075\", \"RFR-0079\", \"RFR-0080\", \"RFR-0081\", \"RFR-0082\", \"RFR-0083\", \"RFR-0084\",\n    \"RFR-0085\", \"RFR-0086\", \"RFR-0087\", \"RFR-0088\", \"RFR-0089\", \"RFR-0090\", \"RFR-0091\",\n    \"RFR-0092\"\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0061\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target 令其传播至附近的敌人 faithfully renders 'causing it to spread to nearby enemies', preserving the spread direction and the 'enemies' restriction; no material defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0062\",\n      \"label\": \"CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_DEFECT\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"The target inserts 选中的 ('selected'), inventing a primary-target/selection mechanic that the source ('causing it to apply instantly when you cast another prophecy') does not contain; the bounded context confirms this detail is invented and that the string is a player-facing talent description, so the defect is established only with context.\",\n      \"defect_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"invented_mechanic\",\n          \"claim\": \"Target adds 选中的预言 ('the selected prophecy'), implying a target-selection mechanic absent from the source's plain 'it ... when you cast another prophecy'.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"source: 'causing it to apply instantly when you cast another prophecy'; target: 令选中的预言在你施放另一个预言时立即生效; bounded context states the 'primary target' detail was invented and is not present in the source.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"source_evidence_sha256s\": [\"bd8180004bdf89556380364e84d685807971803774c5abc36f1db7c69cc453f8\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0063\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Mechanics match runtime: 5-turn black blood on melee hit, once per turn, per-visible-bleeding-creature within 2 grids granting 5%% all resistances capped at %d, scaling with Magic; 暗影伤害 is the standard rendering of darkness damage; the minor leading space and the expanded rendering of 'dark blight' are not material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0064\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target conveys pass-wall movement, per-turn quakes, %d%% increased damage and %d%% increased all resistances, matching inc_damage={all} and resists={all} per the bounded context; 走过墙体 for 'walk through walls' is acceptable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0065\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target states the effect source takes %d%% of the damage the target receives, exactly matching MARK_OF_TREASON's linked_damage = cb.value * eff.power / 100 applied to eff.source; placeholder %d preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0066\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"所有技能冷却时间增加 %d%% preserves the unconditional 'All cooldowns increased by %d%%' with no category exception, matching the bounded context; the added 技能 qualifier is consistent with talent cooldowns.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0067\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target correctly describes the marked target damaging the effect source, which heals for %d%% of that damage, matching Defiled Blood's callbackOnTakeDamage heal of dam * getHeal / 100 on the effect source.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0068\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target matches runtime: debuff removal on application (with the 'other'-type exception supported by context), cooldown reset, per-turn random radius-2 explosion dealing %0.2f darkness and temporal damage and digging diggable walls; placeholders preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0069\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target renders %0.2f void damage per turn, %d%% longer duration on newly applied debuffs (with the context-supported non-'other' restriction), and escalating penalties until removal, matching TOTAL_COLLAPSE behavior.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0070\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target keeps the flat (point) reduction of all non-physical damage while %s is alive, matching flat_damage_armor={all=eff.power, PHYSICAL=-eff.power}; both placeholders preserved with correct referents.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0071\",\n      \"label\": \"SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"The effect name 'Hideous Visions' is rendered as 失智冲击 (approximately 'dementia/insanity shock'), which is semantically unrelated to the English name's meaning of horrifying visions; this mismatch is visible directly from the source/target pair and distorts a player-facing damage-source name.\",\n      \"defect_atoms\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"mistranslated_term\",\n          \"claim\": \"Named effect 'Hideous Visions' is translated as 失智冲击, abandoning the 'visions' (apparitions) meaning entirely and substituting an unrelated 'insanity shock' concept.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"source: 'from Dark Whispers and Hideous Visions'; target: 从黑暗低语和失智冲击中受到额外 %d%% 时空伤害; 'hideous visions' denotes terrifying apparitions, while 失智冲击 denotes a sanity-loss impact, with no 'vision' element retained.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0072\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target correctly places the duration shortening at the end of the suspension (matching EFF_SUSPEND_BEN.deactivate), restricts it to non-'other', non-timeless-decaying detrimental effects, and includes talent cooldown reduction, all supported by the bounded context; 'unable to act, immune to damage' is preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0073\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target matches the Fatebreaker runtime: chosen target dies in the holder's place; Fortune (holder) and Jinx (selected target) stacks are consumed; healing per %d uses selected-target Jinx if present, otherwise holder Fortune — exactly the priority described in the bounded context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0074\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"The target's parentheticals ('only reduced at 1 stack, real increase from 2 stacks'; crit always increased) accurately document the EFF_FORTUNE activate/on_merge asymmetry established by the bounded context, so the added runtime detail is supported and the %d/%d%% placeholders remain correctly bound.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0075\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"The target's additions (first qualifying hit each turn always stuns, later hits roll, same target at most once per turn) are exactly the behavior established by the bounded context from EFF_KROG_WRATH.callbackOnDealDamage and corroborated by the talent tooltip; the base %d%% chance and stun meaning are preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0079\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target conveys the link with the horror ally and %d%% all resistances, matching WTW_SHARED_INSANITY's resists={all=eff.resist} and the resists.all → 全部抗性 terminology mapping.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0080\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target renders empowerment from seeing black blood granting %d%% all resistances, matching SPIKESKIN's resists={all=eff.power} and the resists.all → 全部抗性 terminology.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0081\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target preserves both placeholders ('%d stacks, +%d%% to all damage dealt' → %d 层, +%d%% 所有造成的伤害), consistent with CHAOS_ORBS's beneficial inc_damage={all}; the compressed stat-line phrasing is not a material defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0082\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target renders %d pustules and a %d%% resistance increase; adding 全部 (all) is supported by the bounded context (temporary resists {all=stacks*power}) and matches the resists.all terminology.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0083\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"减少 %d%%所有受到的伤害 preserves the meaning of a %d%% reduction to all damage taken, matching WARBORN's resists={all=eff.power}; the missing space is cosmetic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0084\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target conveys both runtime facts: %d%% reduction to all damage taken and removal of all detrimental effects on application, matching GASTRIC_WAVE_BUFF; the omitted sentence-final period is cosmetic.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0085\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target conveys %d%% reduction to all damage dealt and a 6-turn extension of all detrimental-effect durations on application, matching GASTRIC_WAVE_DEBUFF's inc_damage={all=-eff.power} and duration extension.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0086\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target renders the log as the revelation shortening the named talent's cooldown, which matches the bounded context (alterTalentCoolingdown(tid, -eff.cd) emitted with this log); all three placeholders (%s '%s%s') are preserved in the correct roles.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0087\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Using 虚空之星 (Void Stars) rather than a literal 'void shards' rendering is supported by the bounded context: the code restores Void Stars stacks and the project terminology maps Void Stars=虚空之星, so the target reflects actual runtime and consistent terminology.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0088\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Rendering the effect as the guardian's movement speed increasing is supported by the bounded context (m.movement_speed = m.movement_speed + 0.5 despite the English 'grow in power'); the #CRIMSON# tag and shriek/pen-and-paper imagery are preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0089\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"你需要异变之手！ is a faithful, concise rendering of the player log 'You require a mutated hand!' using the established Mutated Hand=异变之手 terminology; no material defect.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0090\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"Target uses 气之部族 for Atmos, the terminology-correct faction name per the bounded context (replacing the formerly wrong 蒸汽巨人), and 太阳骑士 for Sun Paladins; 'victorious over ... alike' is preserved.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0091\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"快叫人来处理，马上！ correctly conveys 'assign someone to handle it, post-haste' per the bounded context (getting someone to fix the tea-maker), with matching imperative urgency.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"neutral_id\": \"RFR-0092\",\n      \"label\": \"CLEAN\",\n      \"evidence_statement\": \"这只能是阿马克泰尔本人的眼睛！ correctly states the object is Amakthel's own eye, matching the bounded context clarification, and preserves the exclamatory register.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"zai-standard-cn","model":"glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":10622,"output":12106,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":9007,"totalTokens":22728,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1787939357818,"responseId":"20260829014917803be7ea954a4bb3","rawStopReason":"stop"}}
