ich does not correspond to \"hideous visions\" (horrifying apparitions). Hmm, but could \"Hideous Visions\" in this game be a psychic/sanity attack whose Chinese name is a re-interpretation? Translations sometimes localize names freely. But 失智冲击 loses the \"visions\" imagery entirely. I think a material defect is visible: the name no longer conveys \"visions\". I'll go SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT. Actually, careful: labels require \"material defect visible from source and target without relying on bounded context.\" The mismatch of the name is visible. Yes.\n\nHmm, but wait — could this be intentional and standard? Without terminology evidence, the reviewer judges. The name mismatch is stark. I'll go SURFACE_VISIBLE_DEFECT.\n\nRFR-0072: source: \"Each turn, negative effects and cooldowns will decrease in duration.\" Target: \"暂停结束时，非\"其他\"类且不会在无时间状态下自行衰减的负面效果，以及技能冷却时间会缩短。\" Context: EFF_SUSPEND_BEN.deactivate — shortening occurs when Suspend deactivates, iterates effects not tick_on_timeless, detrimental, type not other; subtracts from durations and cooldowns. Target says \"暂停结束时\" (when the pause ends) — matches deactivate. Target adds conditions from runtime. Source says \"Each turn\" but context says it happens at deactivate (once). Target changed \"each turn\" to \"when the suspension ends\" — matches runtime. Also \"无法行动，免疫伤害\" for \"unable to act but unable to take any damage\" — fine. CLEAN. Note: \"negative effects\" → only non-other, non-timeless-decay ones; matches runtime evidence. CLEAN.\n\nRFR-0073: Fatebreaker. Source: \"If it dies, it's chosen target will die in it's place and it will be healed by %d for each stack of Fortune and Jinx.\" Context: consumes holder Fortune and selected target Jinx; healing assigned from holder Fortune first, then overwritten by selected-target Jinx if present. Target: \"此时，自身的幸运层数和所选目标身上的不幸层数会被消耗；若所选目标有不幸，则按其层数治疗，否则按自身的幸运层数治疗，每层恢复 %d 点生命。\" Matches context. Source says \"healed by %d for each stack of Fortune and Jinx\" (ambi